 "notes": "Family: defined-risk NIFTY weekly option spreads held 1-4 days on daily signals, train 2025 only. Step 1, daily pre-check on NIFTY + India VIX daily candles 2012-2024 (16 looks, logged as daily-precheck): a 3-day bull put spread (short ~0.6% OTM, long 200 pts lower at 25k scale, next-open entry, close of day 3 exit, ~3.5 pts costs) priced with Black-Scholes using IV = VIX. Unconditional put spreads ≈ -0.6 pts/trade, bear call spreads negative in every filter (index drift), 'calm' (10d realised vol < VIX) iron-condor legs negative on both sides, so condors and bear calls were dropped. Only one filter stood out: uptrend (close > EMA20, EMA20 rising) AND VIX > SMA20(VIX) AND VIX below yesterday: +7.5 pts/trade (25k scale), 244 signals, t≈2.0, positive in 10 of 13 years but negative in 2012, 2013 and 2016, and concentrated in 2021-2024. Fragile: the SMA10 VIX-mean variant drops to +2.3 pts, t 0.9. Step 2, one engine screen offline (1 look) only to confirm the signal dates (17 of 17 skipped for missing option data, as expected). Step 3, two online training experiments with identical rules: E0041 NIFTY and E0042 SENSEX (replication), each with a 2x-slippage stress period. Each made 11 trades in 2025 (0 skipped): NIFTY +₹2.8k, PF 1.19, t 0.22, net without the top trades -₹0.8k, H1 -₹6.2k / H2 +₹9.0k; SENSEX +₹1.9k, PF 1.14, t 0.15, H1 -₹5.6k / H2 +₹7.5k. Both still slightly positive at 2x slippage (+₹1.1k / +₹1.4k). Margin (max loss) is ~₹11-13k per lot, return on peak margin 21% / 16%. One trade (entry 3 Apr 2025, the tariff gap-down of 7 Apr) lost ~₹11k on each index, about the whole spread width; the other 10 are small wins. That is the textbook short-put payoff, and 11 trades a year can't tell an edge from luck. Verdict: nothing meets the training bar (min 20 trades, t ≥ 2), so no candidates are submitted. The rule is listed under 'watchlist' (not auto-queued) in case the lead wants a low-frequency, defined-risk bullish sleeve for a bucket. The third experiment was deliberately not used: loosening the filter to get more trades had a weak prior in the pre-check (VIX high & falling without the trend filter: +1.75 pts, t 0.9), so it would have been mining.",
